    "created_at": "2017-09-13T23:43:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-13T23:45:09Z",
    "body": "There is no practical alternative to input type number in iOS safari and android chrome that will bring up the appropriate keyboard.  Specifying which keyboard should be used by mobile browsers is by far the most important practical use of input types.\r\n\r\nI see in the spec the note that 'The type=number state is not appropriate for input that happens to only consist of numbers but isn’t strictly speaking a number.', but number inputs are widely used for credit card numbers (by stripe, amazon, etc..) because of the lack of alternatives.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
